SWEET Bluetooth: patch 0296 (bt/defaults 2026-11-11), the controller bring-up runs off the boot path. sweet_bt_uart_attach used to run the patchram download (about 42 s at 115200 baud, 3038 x 0xfc4c records), lefeat (0274) and the VSC capability read (0285) before launchd started [obs logs/runs/20261110T174143Z-bt-pr2: patchram start 1794332642.355, verified 1794332684.173, first exec launchd 1794332685.083]; with 0295 making that default ON it would add about 42 s to every boot. Now attach starts one kernel thread (sbu_bringup_thread) and returns: the thread runs the SAME call chain in the same order (sbu_patchram_attach, sbu_rfwit_knob, sbu_attach_finish) and then becomes the rx loop, so the rx poll never runs against a half-initialised controller and no controller command, register or bus store is new. While the thread runs, sweet_bt_uart_bringup_busy() is 1 and sbt_connect refuses every kctl client (plain and sk control) with EBUSY and one bounded `BT GAP:` row (BlueTool answers result 1, bluetoothd retries boot). Rows: `BT UART: bring-up done in N ms (async)`; failure paths keep their GAP rows. If kernel_thread_start fails the bring-up runs synchronously (one GAP). Applies after 0295.

